 "title": "Comparative Analysis of RNA Assembly Methods and Tools",
 "summary": "This cluster focuses on various methods and tools for RNA assembly, including StringTie1 and StringTie2, which are used to assemble transcripts from RNA sequencing data. StringTie2 is shown to be faster and more accurate than FLAIR and Scallop, and it replaces the bit-vector representation. The splicing graph pruning algorithm uses several genes, including C1orf174, COL1A1, uc060qvn.1, and uc284pkq.1. Third-generation sequencing technologies, such as Oxford Nanopore and PacBio, use this algorithm and have an error profile. FLAIR is shown to perform better than Traphlor, and StringTie2 is also better than Traphlor.",
